I"#<h2 id="about-the-book">About the Book</h2>

<p>Every large IT organization faces a common enemy: complexity. As systems grow, teams scale, and cloud services multiply, the cognitive and operational burden of keeping everything running becomes a drag on innovation and agility.</p>

<p><em>Overcoming IT Complexity</em> provides a practical roadmap for simplifying your IT environment — not by slowing down, but by making deliberate architectural choices that reduce accidental complexity and let your teams focus on what matters.</p>

<h2 id="what-youll-learn">What You’ll Learn</h2>

<ul>
  <li>How to identify and classify the sources of complexity in your systems</li>
  <li>Strategies for reducing technical debt without stalling product development</li>
  <li>Cloud architecture patterns that prioritize simplicity and long-term maintainability</li>
  <li>Organizational approaches that reduce operational overhead and toil</li>
  <li>How to build a culture of simplicity that sustains itself as teams and systems grow</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="who-this-book-is-for">Who This Book Is For</h2>

<p>Technology leaders, architects, and senior engineers in organizations running complex cloud infrastructure who want practical frameworks for making their systems more manageable and their teams more effective.</p>
